    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186768": {
      "title": "FA27-018: Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor in Computer Science / Cybersecurity Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-03 Deadline: 2027-01-15 Location: Edwardsville, IL The Department of Computer Science at Southern Illinois University Edwardsville (SIUE) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position, primarily in support of the Cybersecurity Engineering program. The Cybersecurity Engineering program is an interdisciplinary program bridging Computer Science and Computer Engineering. The Cybersecurity Engineering program is a new program, and the opportunity is available for a qualified candidate to serve as Program Director.  As part of the SIUE School of Engineering, the Computer Science Department offers an ABET-accredited B.S. degree program in Computer Science, as well as B.A. and M.S. Computer Science degree programs, and the B.S in Cybersecurity Engineering. The Electrical and Computer Engineering Department offers ABET-accredited B.S. degrees in Electrical Engineering and Computer Engineering and an M.S. degree in Electrical and Computer Engineering. The School of Engineering is committed to attracting, supporting, and retaining employees with all identities and backgrounds, and particularly candidates form underrepresented groups in STEM such as women faculty and faculty of color. SIUE faculty are encouraged to contribute to inclusive excellence in both the academic community and region through research, teaching, and service. Salary Assistant Professor     $98,000-$104,000 Associate Professor    $116,000-$126,000 Professor                     $141,000-$158,000 Terms of Appointment Full-time, continuing, tenure-eligible appointment beginning August 2027 Source of Funds State A Ph.D. in computer science, electrical/computer engineering, or related area is required. ABD candidates may be considered. All applicants must have a demonstrated interest in teaching and mentoring in computer science and cybersecurity, at both the undergraduate and graduate level. Applicants must have a demonstrated interest in developing a quality research program and in attracting external research funding. Submit a letter of application that includes a research statement, a statement on teaching philosophy, a curriculum vitae, and contact information for at least three references. Application Deadline Application materials will be accepted until January 15, 2027 or until position is filled. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States. This offer of employment will be rescinded in the event that you fail to secure legal rights to employability in the United States. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "School of Engineering"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184335": {
      "title": "FA27-004: Lecturer, Continuing Open Recruitment",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-26 Deadline: 2027-06-30 Location: Edwardsville, IL The SIUE School of Nursing is accepting resume packages for various part-time, non-tenure, semester term appointments for the 2026-2027 academic year.  This listing does not represent an actual vacancy; rather open recruitment allows interested persons to submit materials for future vacancies within the grad school. Positions may be in various major areas and teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate or graduate programs at the Edwardsville campuses. The SIUE School of Nursing offers a diverse, vibrant, supportive environment. Students learn excellence in nursing leadership through: -innovative teaching; -quality research; -community service; -and compassionate care in this diverse and complex world. The SIUE School of Nursing programs prepare students for a fast-paced, rapidly evolving career in health care at a time when the country is facing a nursing shortage. Surrounding hospitals and health care centers heavily recruit our nursing graduates due to their commitment to outstanding patient care.  Learn more at: https://www.siue.edu/nursing/ Terms of Appointment Semester term appointment % varies Source of Funds State Master’s of Science in Nursing required; doctorate preferred. Two (2) years of experience in clinical nursing. Doctorate (PhD, EdD, DNS, DNSc, DNP) is required for any graduate faculty position. Previous teaching experience in a baccalaureate program and research experience preferred but not required. Pediatrics, maternal child, public health, medical-surgical, nurse practitioner, health care informatics, nursing administration, or school nurse education and experience is highly desirable. Practice experience in the specialty area being applied for is required as is RN licensure in Illinois and Missouri. Programs are CCNE accredited. Submit a letter of application, resume, academic transcripts, and current contact information for three professional references. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "School of Nursing"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184336": {
      "title": "FA27-005: Nurse Anethesia/Lecturer, Continuing Open Recruitment",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-26 Deadline: 2027-06-30 Location: Edwardsville, IL The SIUE School of Nursing is accepting resume packages for various part-time, non-tenure, semester term appointments for the 2025-2026 academic year. This listing does not represent an actual vacancy; rather open recruitment allows interested persons to submit materials for future vacancies within the school. These positions will include teaching responsibilities in graduate programs in the area of Nurse Anesthesia. The SIUE School of Nursing offers a diverse, vibrant, supportive environment. Students learn excellence in nursing leadership through: -innovative teaching; -quality research; -community service; -and compassionate care in this diverse and complex world. The SIUE School of Nursing programs prepare students for a fast-paced, rapidly evolving career in health care at a time when the country is facing a nursing shortage. Surrounding hospitals and health care centers heavily recruit our nursing graduates due to their commitment to outstanding patient care. Learn more at: https://www.siue.edu/nursing/ Terms of Appointment Semester term appointment % varies Source of Funds State Candidates for these positions must have a Master’s of Science in Nursing, doctorate is preferred. Doctorate (PhD, EdD, DNS, DNSc, DNP) is required for any graduate faculty position. Two years’ clinical experience in specialty area being applied for is required.  Previous teaching experience in a baccalaureate nursing program is preferred, but not required. RN licensure in Illinois and Missouri is required. Submit a letter of application, resume, academic transcripts (unofficial are permissible for application review purposes), and current contact information for three professional references. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "School of Nursing"
