    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190757": {
      "title": "FA27-024: Director of IRIS Center for Digital Humanities and Social Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-29 Deadline: 2026-09-30 Location: Edwardsville, IL Position Overview Southern Illinois University Edwardsville (SIUE) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty member to serve as the Director of the IRIS Center for Digital Humanities and Social Sciences. The Director will oversee the Center’s operations and support its growth and development through building and extending campus and community partnerships, writing grants, and leading project development with faculty and students. The successful candidate, with a demonstrated background in digital humanities and social sciences scholarship, will hold a joint appointment in an appropriate academic department in the College of Arts and Sciences and will teach courses central to the Center’s curricular mission. About the IRIS Center Since its founding in 2010, the IRIS Center has grown into one of SIUE’s most distinctive academic centers. The Center has secured more than $5 million in grants from state, federal, and private sources and is a primary technical and pedagogical partner for the Community-Oriented Digital Engagement Scholars (CODES) program, an award-winning initiative integrating community-engaged curriculum and digital storytelling that supports first-generation, Pell-eligible, and historically underrepresented students. The Center administers an interdisciplinary Digital Humanities and Social Sciences (DHSS) Minor and partners with the Black Literary Network, a project supported by a $1.5 million Mellon Foundation grant. The successful candidate will lead IRIS during an exciting period of growth as the University advances the Center to full Center status, providing an opportunity to shape its future vision, expand interdisciplinary collaborations, and build on its record of external funding and public impact. Key Responsibilities Provide strategic vision, day-to-day operational management, and budget administration for the IRIS Center. Lead staff and coordinate Center activities, ensuring adequate coverage across research, pedagogy, and outreach functions. Collaborate with other university Centers, academic, and administrative units to foster and support faculty and student DH research and pedagogy and cultivate regional partnerships that extend the Center’s impact beyond campus. Serve as Technical Director for the CODES program, developing curricula, tutorials, and digital learning resources and planning and managing the CODES ePortfolio platform and the program’s publishing platform, Emplace . Teach HUM 230: Introduction to Digital Humanities and HUM 490: Digital Creation and Storytelling. Write, submit, and manage grant applications from state, federal, and private sources to sustain and grow Center programming. Terms of Appointment Souce of Funds State PhD in a humanities or social sciences discipline. Demonstrated expertise in digital humanities tools, methods, and scholarly practice. Evidence of, or clear potential for successful grant writing and procuring external funding via grants and contracts. Experience or demonstrated capacity in project management and budget administration. Commitment to mentoring and supporting undergraduate and graduate students, including those from historically underrepresented populations. Strong cross-disciplinary and community outreach experience or potential. Preferred Qualifications Record of interdisciplinary collaboration spanning humanities and social sciences. Experience directing or co-directing an academic center, lab, or comparable unit. Experience with the public humanities, community-engaged scholarship, or related fields. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive pedagogy and student success initiatives Application Deadline All application materials must be received by September 30, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, please submit: (1) a cover letter addressing qualifications and vision for the IRIS Center, (2) a current curriculum vitae, (3) a teaching philosophy statement, 4) research statement) 5) copies of transcripts, and 6) current contact information for three references. This institution is using Interfolio’s Faculty Search to conduct this search. Applicants to this position receive a free dossier account and can send all application materials, including confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Please address questions about this position to Dr. Howard Rambsy, hrambsy@siue.edu. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "IRIS Center"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173790": {
      "title": "FA26-024: Program Coordinator/Instructor Surveying and Geomatics",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-11-17 Location: Edwardsville, IL Southern Illinois University Edwardsville (SIUE) is seeking an experienced and dedicated surveyor (Professional Land Surveyor (PLS) preferred) to serve as Surveying and Geomatics Program Director within the School of Engineering. This position provides leadership and oversight for the university’s Surveying and Geomatics Program, ensuring academic excellence, program growth, and alignment with professional standards and industry needs. The ideal candidate will bring a balance of practical field experience, proven leadership ability, and a genuine passion for teaching and mentoring. The Program Director will be an approachable, relatable leader who can effectively connect with students, faculty, and professionals while guiding the program’s continued development and success. The successful candidate will also teach courses in the Surveying and Geomatics program within the Department of Construction of the School of Engineering.  Teaching assignments may include online, evening, weekend, and satellite courses.  Summer assignments are available subject to enrollment and funding. The successful candidate will: • Provide strategic leadership and daily management for the Surveying and Geomatics Program, including curriculum oversight, assessment, scheduling, and program development. • Teach undergraduate and certificate program courses in surveying and geomatics, integrating practical field knowledge with classroom instruction. • Mentor and advise students, fostering their academic and professional growth. • Recruit, supervise, and support faculty and staff within the program. • Build and maintain strong partnerships with industry, professional organizations, and community stakeholders. • Ensure the program meets and maintains accreditation standards and reflects current technologies and practices in the surveying profession. • Manage program budgets, resources, and marketing/outreach efforts to promote enrollment and visibility. • Represent SIUE’s Surveying Program at professional conferences, regional events, and advisory boards. Term of Appointment Source of Funds State Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have a Baccelaurate degree (B.S.) in Surveying, Geomatics, Civil Engineering, or a closely related field with approximately 5 years of experience and active State licensure in Surveying and Geomatics. Applicants must have significant field experience in land surveying. Applicants must have demonstrated managerial or supervisory experience. Applicants must have clearly demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching, mentoring, and engaged service to the program. Applicants must have demonstratable knowledge of modern surveying equipment, GPS, scanning, sonar equipment, and pre and post processing of data collection software, with the ability to transmit data into AutoCAD and MicroStation, and other software. Applicants must demonstrate that they have knowledge, skill, and demonstrated commitment to anti-racism, diversity, equity, and inclusion. Preferred Qualifications Active participation in professional surveying associations (e.g., IPLSA, NSPS, MSPS). At least two years as a distinct leader. Skill in mentoring and advising students. Skill in field-based learning. Skill in on-line and certificate program learning. Experience with program accreditation, curriculum design, or academic assessment. Readiness to cooperate on shared responsibilities in a department with a commitment to collaboration. Submit letter of application, resume, transcipts, and references. Application Deadline Position open until filled. Initial review January 2026. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "Construction"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/173382": {
      "title": "FA26-020: Chair, Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-11-10 Location: Edwardsville, IL The Chair of the Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences will provide inspirational and visionary leadership and strategic direction for the department, recruit, mentor, and support faculty and staff to achieve excellence in teaching, research, and service; foster a collaborative inclusive, and innovative departmental culture; promote and support high-impact, externally funded research programs in pharmaceutical and administrative sciences; oversee departmental operations, including budgeting, personnel management, curriculum development, and assessment; collaborate with other department chair, school and university leadership, and external partners to advance the mission of the School of Pharmacy; advocate for departmental needs within the school and university; teach and contribute to the academic programs of the school, including PharmD, MS, and PhD education; engage in professional and community service consistent with university and school goals; and, maintain scholarly research endeavors. Terms of Appointment 12-month continuing appointment Source of Funds State Minimum Qualifications terminal degree (PhD or equivalent) in Pharmaceutical Sciences or closely related discipline a distinguished record of teaching, scholarship, and service achievement, commensurate with appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Full Professor and be eligible for tenure demonstrated leadership experience in academic and/or research settings proven ability to secure and manage extramural research funding strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills scholarship within one of the field(s) of medicinal chemistry, pharmaceutics, pharmacology, or social and administrative sciences Additional Beneficial Qualifications experience in academic administration or past service as department chair, center director, or program leader experience in curriculum development and accreditation processes understanding of and commitment to interprofessional education and research experience mentoring faculty, postdocs, and students ongoing extramural funding Submit letter of intent detailing interest in the position and relevant experience, curriculum vitae, statement of educational and administrative philosophy, and names and contact information for three references (references will not be contacted without candidate permission.) SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "School of Pharmacy"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/175173": {
      "title": "FA26-028: Assistant Professor, Social and Administrative Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-17 Location: Edwardsville, IL Provide instruction in the Doctor of Pharmacy Program. Serve as Course coordinator/instructor as appropriate. Conduct independent research in their area of interest with the goal of developing a record of scholarly pursuit and expertise. Engage in service (School, University, Professional, and Community) Mentor students. Other duties as assigned. Terms of Appointment 12-month continuing appointment Source of Funds State Candidates should possess a Ph.D. in Social and Administrative Sciences, Health Economics, Pharmacy Administration or a closely related area (examples include health services research, health outcomes, health policy, translational science). Individuals with a MS and Pharm.D. or Pharm. D. degree with two-year fellowship in Pharmacoeconomics/Health Outcomes Research or population-based care with a history of publications are also encouraged to apply.  Applicants should demonstrate strength in one of more of the following areas: population-based care, health economics, health outcomes, community-based participatory research, or implementation sciences.  A background in pharmacy is preferred, but not required. Submit a letter of intent in the position, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching or research philosophy, and names and contact information for three references (references will be contacted without candidate permission. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "School of Pharmacy"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/184549": {
      "title": "FA27-007: Pharmacy Practice Lecturer, Part-Time, Continuous",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-01 Deadline: 2027-06-30 Location: Edwardsville, IL The School of Pharmacy, Department of Pharmacy Practice is accepting resume packages for part-time, non-tenure, semester term appointments for the 2026-2027 academic year. This listing does not represent an actual vacancy; rather open recruitment allows interested persons to submit materials for future vacancies with the School of Pharmacy. These non-tenure track faculty positions may be in the practice areas (depending on needs): patient communications; physical and patient assessment; inpatient/acute care; ambulatory patient care; community pharmacy; self-care; pharmacotherapeutics; health literacy and disparities; as well as clinical reasoning and shared decision making. Needs for academic year 2026-2027 include: first and third (P1 and P3) year practice skills course series (Tuesdays or Wednesdays, weekly during the semester), Patient-Centered Communication (Mondays and Thursdays), and occasional lectures and teaching assistance in other courses. Lecturers will prepare for and lead at least one section of the class as well as contribute to course coordination activities as part of the course instructor team. In the Pharmacy School students learn the knowledge, skills, and attitudes of a practicing pharmacist in preparation for patient care practice. Faculty teach and conduct scholarly research on optimal instruction to prepare competent pharmacists for practice. In our work, we seek to model and promote ethical and equitable patient care as well as inclusive excellence. We are an educational community dedicated to the preparation of pharmacy professionals, scholars and leaders to improve the health and well-being of our region and beyond. Terms of Appointment Academic term, appointment % varies Source of Funds State PharmD degree and eligibility for licensure as a pharmacist in the state of Illinois is required for all faculty positions. Candidates should support our mission to serve patients in central and southern Illinois, especially those in underserved communities. Experience in precepting or teaching students or residents is preferred. Interested applicants should submit a letter of application, academic transcripts, and references. Candidates interested in positions should first communicate with the department chair about availability and needs of such positions. See: https://www.siue.edu/pharmacy/departments-faculty-staff/bio-hookstra-jennifer.shtml Application Deadline We will accept applications throughout the year and will continue to review applications based on position availability and departmental need. This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier account and can send all application materials, including confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "School of Pharmacy"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/179014": {
      "title": "FA26-041: Assistant/Associate Professor (depending upon qualifications)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-02 Location: Alton, IL The Southern Illinois University School of Dental Medicine is seeking applications for a full-time tenure track position at the Assistant/Associate/Full Professor level in the Department of Biomedical and Craniofacial Sciences. This position is in behavioral sciences as pertains to clinical dentistry. This includes didactic instruction as well as support of clinical training and assessment in the application of fundamental principles of behavioral sciences to patient care including interpersonal skills and behavioral/psychological approaches to management of dental patients, communication skills, anxiety, and pain control, etc. Responsibilities include teaching in the predoctoral and postdoctoral programs, as well as independent research and service to the University. Working in collaboration with other faculty, both in research and in teaching, is encouraged. Salary Range: Biomedical Faculty Assistant Professor   $85,000 - $95,000 Associate Professor  $95,000 - $105,000 Professor                  $105,000 - $115,000 Clinical Dentistry (DMD, DDS) Faculty Assistant Professor / Clinical Assistant Professor     $120,000 - $130,000 Associate Professor / Clinical Associate Professor   $130,000 - $140,000 Professor / Clinical Professor                                          $140,000 - $150,000 Terms of Appointment Academic Source of Funds State This position requires a Ph.D. or equivalent degree in a behavioral science field such as psychology, psychiatry, communication studies, or social work and has expertise in behavioral health or health sciences education. Experience integrating behavioral health principles into patient care is desirable. Alternatively, a D.M.D., D.D.S. or equivalent degree with strong foundational training and interest in behavioral sciences would be considered (in which case applicants must be licensed to practice dentistry in the state of Illinois, or be able to meet the requirements for Illinois licensure). Previous teaching experience and/or a record of research accomplishments through publication and external funding are desirable. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, and three letters of reference. Application Deadline The position will remain open until filled. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "Department of Biomedical and Craniofacial Sciences"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186570": {
      "title": "FA27-009: Adjunct Lecturer, Continuing Open Recruitment for Summer 2026 and AY2026-2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-01 Deadline: 2027-06-30 Location: Edwardsville, IL The Adjunct Lecturer will teach instructional services in support of the Center for Predictive Analytics initiatives. The Adjunct Lecturer will provide instructional services to participants for adult basic education, employability and personal development skills, and digital literacy. The Adjunct Lecturer will also provide the CPAN leadership team with monthly updates on program progress, barriers, and promising practices. All qualified applicants will consist of a pool from which appointments will be made on an as-needed basis. Terms of Appointment Continuing, Open Recruitment Source of Funds Federal Bachelor’s Degree is required with relevant experience or reentry experience. Master's degree preferred but not required. Excellent written and verbal communication skills are required for this position. Previous teaching experience preferred but not required. Submit letter of application, resume, transcripts, and three references. Application Deadline Closing date for applications is June 30, 2027. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "Center for Predictive Analytics"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190758": {
      "title": "FA27-025: Research Faculty Fellow - Data Analyst (3 Positions)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31 Deadline: 2026-09-30 Location: Edwardsville, IL The Center for Predictive Analytics (C-PAN) at Southern Illinois University Edwardsville (SIUE) is committed to fostering the pursuit of multidisciplinary scholarly research that is supported by data-driven insights. In response to this mission, C-PAN is soliciting applications for three analyst positions that will support quantitative and mixed methods data analysis, program evaluation, data acquisition and curation, and secure data handling strategies across the SIUE campus. Specifically, the individuals hired for these positions will assist faculty members across the SIUE campus in carrying out the analytical and data-intensive portions of their projects. The positions cover the various aspects of mixed methods analysis, policy and resource analysis, experimental design, quantitative data analysis, and secure data management and processing. For more information regarding the three positions, please see Qualifications. Terms of Appointment Source of Funds Local Mixed Methods Data Analyst Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in a STEM discipline or a quantitatively-intensive social science field. At least 6 months of experience teaching in a classroom or online learning environment. Knowledge of experimental design and analysis, natural language processing, and discriminative and generative artificial intelligence models. At least 1 year of experience working with R, Python, or SAS. At least 6 months of experience serving as an instructor for traditional or non-traditional/alternative credentialing programs (e.g., microcredentials). Knowledge of secure data handling procedures for confidential and anonymous data. Desired Skills Master’s degree or higher in a related discipline. Demonstrated knowledge of student-centered educational practices. Fluency in R, Python, or SAS. Policy and Capital Resources Data Analyst Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Geography/GIS, Environmental Sciences, Political Science, Public Policy, or a similar discipline with experience in geospatial analysis and policy analysis. At least one year of experience working with GIS tools. Experience working with geographical analyses with human, policy, and/or geopolitical components. Experience aggregating data from multiple databases into a unified source for analysis. Desired Skills Master’s degree or higher in related discipline. Knowledge of experimental design and analysis, natural language processing, and discriminative and generative artificial intelligence models. At least one year of experience working with Python or R. Knowledge of secure data handling procedures for confidential and anonymous data. Quantitative Data Analyst and Automation Specialist Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a STEM or quantitatively-intensive discipline. At least 6 months of experience creating automated workflows in Power Automate. Knowledge of experimental design and analysis, natural language processing, and discriminative and generative artificial intelligence models. At least 6 months’ experience working with Python, R, or SAS. Experience aggregating data from multiple databases into a unified source for analysis. Desired Skills Master’s degree or higher in related discipline. Fluency in Python, R, or SAS. At least 1 year of experience working with GIS tools. Experience creating AI agents for targeted applications. Knowledge of secure data handling procedures and data management protocols. Submit cover letter, resume or CV, unofficial transcript(s), and the contact information for three references. Personal statements that describe research, clinical, consulting, teaching, and/or other relevant experience are also welcome. Questions should be directed to Ms. Dixie Butts at dibutts@siue.edu. Application Deadline Closing date for applications is 09/30/2026. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "Center for Predictive Analytics"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191313": {
      "title": "FA27-026: Postdoctoral Research Faculty Fellow",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09 Deadline: 2026-10-08 Location: Edwardsville, IL The Geospatial Mapping, Applications, and Research Center (GeoMARC) at Southern Illinois University Edwardsville invites applications for a two-year Research Faculty Fellow (Postdoctoral Scholar) appointment in Remote Sensing and Environmental Analytics. GeoMARC has a long history of conducting applied research for federal and state agencies, utility providers, agricultural organizations, and private industry partners, with projects focused on environmental monitoring, environmental quality assessment, natural resource management, and geospatial decision support. Current research utilizes satellite, airborne, uncrewed aerial systems (UAS), and LiDAR data to address challenges related to agriculture, energy infrastructure, biodiversity, land-use change, ecosystem monitoring, and environmental sustainability. The successful candidate will contribute expertise in remote sensing, image analysis, machine learning, and AI-driven geospatial technologies to support and advance a diverse portfolio of externally funded research and applied geospatial projects. Working closely with GeoMARC ‘s highly experienced research team, the Research Faculty Fellow will contribute to the development of innovative analytical approaches and workflows that help transform remotely sensed data into actionable information for environmental decision-making and resource management. The Research Faculty Fellow will also be provided with the opportunity to work closely with GeoMARC’s faculty to synthesize findings from past and ongoing projects into peer-reviewed publications, technical reports, and conference presentations. Through exposure to (and participation in) a broad range of active research initiatives, the Fellow will gain extensive experience applying remote sensing, image analysis, machine learning, and geospatial technologies to real-world environmental challenges while building a strong publication record and developing a comprehensive understanding of GeoMARC's research mission, methodologies, and partnerships. Building on this experience, the Fellow will contribute to the continued growth of GeoMARC by helping identify emerging research opportunities and funding initiatives related to the use of remote sensing and geospatial analysis for environmental monitoring, environmental quality, agriculture, and energy-sector applications. Working alongside GeoMARC’s leadership, the Fellow will assist in the development of competitive grant proposals and collaborative research partnerships while gaining valuable experience in sponsored research development and the operation of a multidisciplinary applied research center. Terms of Appointment Source of Funds Ph.D. in Geography, Environmental Science, Remote Sensing, Geospatial Science, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Demonstrated expertise in remote sensing, digital image processing, and machine learning, particularly as applied to environmental monitoring, environmental quality assessment, land-use and land-cover change analysis, and landscape-scale feature detection. Demonstrated experience working with satellite remote sensing data (e.g., Planet Labs, Sentinel, Landsat) and UAS-based remote sensing data, including RGB, multispectral, and LiDAR datasets. Proficiency with ArcGIS Pro, Google Earth Engine, and ERDAS IMAGINE or comparable image processing and geospatial analysis software. Strong proficiency in Python programming, with experience developing automated geospatial workflows and processing large geospatial datasets. Strong quantitative and statistical skills, including experience with sampling design, model development, validation procedures, accuracy assessment, and uncertainty analysis. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines in a collaborative, applied research environment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare technical reports, peer-reviewed publications, grant proposals, and professional presentations. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of vegetation ecology, plant community characteristics, and environmental monitoring applications. Experience developing and implementing machine learning and deep learning approaches for classification, regression, object detection, or predictive modeling. Experience evaluating model performance through pre-modeling data assessment, feature selection, validation, and post-modeling accuracy and uncertainty analyses. Demonstrated experience preparing research proposals, managing externally funded projects, or contributing to interdisciplinary research teams. FAA Part 107 Remote Pilot Certification or the ability to obtain certification within six months of appointment. Submit cover letter, resume, transcript, and three professional references. Application deadline is October 9, 2026 . Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "GeoMARC"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/176498": {
      "title": "FA26-036: Lecturer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-01-16 Location: Edwardsville, IL Periodically, the John Martinson Honors Program may have various openings throughout the year for part-time, non-tenure, semester term Lecturer appointments. For more information on specific offerings in the Program, please visit: https://www.siue.edu/provost/honors/ . SIUE is committed to education that explores the historic significance of diversity in order to understand the present and to better enable our community to engage the future. Terms of Appointment Academic, term position beginning fall 2026, spring 2027 Source of Funds State An advanced degree in discipline of instruction (or equivalent professional experience in Fine Arts) is required. Submit resume and transcripts. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to offer of employment. Application Deadline The Honors Program will accept applications throughout the year and will continue to review applications based on position availability. For timely review, application review for each semester begins: 1 April 2026 for Fall 2026 1 October 2026 for Spring 2027 SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu . The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "John Martinson Honors Program"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182285": {
      "title": "FA27-001: Lecturer, Continuing Open Recruitment for AY26/27 and Summer 2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-27 Deadline: 2027-06-30 Location: Edwardsville, IL The SIUE School of Business is accepting resume packages for non-tenure eligible part-time, lecturers for the 2026-2027 academic year. This listing does not represent an actual vacancy; rather open recruitment allows interested persons to submit materials for future vacancies within the School of Business. These non-tenure eligible faculty positions will teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Accounting, Business Statistics, Computer Management & Information Systems, Economics, Finance, Management, and Marketing. Lecturers will take responsibility as instructor of record for all elements of courses including delivering lectures, grading assignments, and supporting students as needed. The School of Business is among an elite five percent of business schools worldwide that have earned the prestigious accreditation from the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). This accreditation represents the highest standard of achievement for business schools worldwide. Less than 25 percent of AACSB-accredited schools also hold the accounting accreditation. The School of Business has been accredited by AACSB since 1975, and the accountancy program achieved separate accreditation in 1987. Terms of Appointment Academic, term position beginning fall 2026, spring 2027, and/or summer 2027 Source of Funds State Applicants must have a Master's degree in a related field and must have five (5) recent years of significant business-related experience in the discipline for which they are applying. Faculty must maintain AACSB qualifications through ongoing work experience or faculty development activities. Submit a letter of application, resume, transcripts, and references. Please reference courses/areas of interest and/or specialty. Application Deadline Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will continue to be reviewed based on departmental and school needs. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "Office of the School of Business"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182286": {
      "title": "FA27-002: Facilitator, Continuing Open Recruitment for AY26/27 and Summer 2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-27 Deadline: 2027-06-30 Location: Edwardsville, IL The School of Business is accepting resume packages for part-time non-tenure eligible facilitators for the 2026-2027 academic year. This listing does not represent an actual vacancy; rather open recruitment allows interested persons to submit materials for future vacancies within the School of Business. These non­ tenure eligible facilitators will assist faculty with undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Accounting, Business Statistics, Computer Management & Information Systems, Economics, Finance, Management and Marketing. Facilitators are not the instructor of record and do not deliver course material. Responsibilities may include facilitating class discussion, grading assignments, and/or supporting the faculty member of record as needed. The School of Business is among an elite five percent of business schools worldwide that have earned the prestigious accreditation from the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB International). This accreditation represents the highest standard of achievement for business schools worldwide. Less than 25 percent of AACSB-accredited schools also hold the accounting accreditation. The School of Business has been accredited by AACSB since 1975, and the accountancy program achieved separate accreditation in 1987. Terms of Appointment Academic, term position beginning fall 2026, spring 2027, and/or summer 2027 Source of Funds State Applicants must have a Master's degree in a related field and must have at least one (1) recent post-graduate year of significant business-related experience in the discipline for which they are applying. Submit a letter of application, resume, transcripts, and references. Please reference courses/areas of interest and/or specialty. Application Deadline Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will continue to be reviewed based on departmental and school needs. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "Office of the School of Business"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/182284": {
      "title": "FA27-003: Lecturer, Continuing Open Recruitment for AY2026-2027 and Summer 2027",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-27 Deadline: 2027-06-30 Location: Edwardsville, IL The SIUE School of Education, Health and Human Behavior is accepting resume packages for part-time, non-tenure, semester term Lecturer position openings for the 2026-2027 academic year. This listing does not represent an actual vacancy; rather open recruitment allows interested persons to submit materials for future vacancies within the School of Education, Health, and Human Behavior. These non-tenure track faculty positions may be in the program areas: Elementary Education, Secondary Education, Early Childhood Education, Special Education, Educational Administration, Higher Education Student Affairs, Information Technology, Psychology, Speech Pathology and Audiology, Exercise Physiology, Exercise Science, Nutrition, Exercise and Sports Psychology, and Public Health. In the School of Education, Health and Human Behavior (SEHHB), students can learn about human thriving from many perspectives. SEHHB faculty and staff teach about, and do research on, healthy living, optimal instruction and learning, and improving organizations. In all their work, they seek to model and promote equitable practices and inclusive excellence.  For more information on the School of Education, Health and Human Behavior, visit us online at: https://www.siue.edu/education/ Terms of Appointment Academic term, appointment % varies Source of Funds State Ph.D. is preferred. Master’s and Specialist’s with specific expertise will be considered. Submit a letter of application, resume, academic transcripts, and references. Application Deadline The departments will accept applications throughout the year and will continue to review applications based on position availability and departmental need. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "Office of the School of Education"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/186511": {
      "title": "FA27-027: IEP English Lecturer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04 Deadline: 2026-11-29 Location: Edwardsville, IL The English Lecturer will work with the director of the IEP to implement and teach effective and engagning program curricula to incoming international English language learners who have not yet met SIUE's proficiency requirements for direct entry into their degree programs. The program will offer two levels of English learning to accommodate for learners' varying English skills, which will prepare them for success in academic coursework at SIUE. Levels taught fall within the CEFR scale of B1. Responsibilities will include: 12 OR 24 hours of on-campus teaching per week (based on student enrollment, program classes offered, and/or the lecturer's schedule preference), lesson planning and grading as required per each class's curriculum. Terms of Appointment Spring 2027 semester, with job duties beginning on January 4th, 2027 Source of Funds State Bachlor's degree from an accredited institution in the U.S. Evidence of a strong sense of pedagogical skills and thoughtful strategies Minimum of one year of ESL teaching experience Experience with diverst, multi-cultural people and cultures U.S. citizen or permanent resident Availability: Mondays-Thursdays from 10am-4pm and Fridays from 10am-3pm. (Actual teaching hours could be less. However, candidates must be available to teach every weekday M-F.) Please submit cover letter, resume, transcripts, and three references. Applicants will be subject to a background check prior to an offer of employment. Employment is contingent upon satisfying all legal requirements as set forth by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services in regard to employability in the United States.  SIUE makes no representation, warranty, or agreement that third parties, including government agencies, will approve submitted documents, applications, or petitions for an H-1B visa or Optional Practical Training. SIUE is a state university - benefits under state sponsored plans may not be available to holders of F1 or J1 visas. The State of Illinois requires that immigrant employees achieve H-1 status before they become eligible for certain benefits. In compliance with the ADA Amendments Acts (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Southern Illinois University Edwardsville, please call 618-650-2190 or email CareerInfo@siue.edu. The SIUE Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available online at https://www.siue.edu/police/cleary-act-forms/ . This report is published in compliance the “Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act” and the Higher Education Opportunity Act also known as the “Campus Fire Safety Right to Know.”",
      "department": "Grad & International Admission"
    }
